# Commit, merge, release, deploy

Work is done only when it is live. Full detail: `AGENTS.md`, "Definition of done" and "Deploying to Cloudron".

1. Run the checks: `composer ci:check` (and `npm run build` if the frontend changed).
2. In the PR, move the change from `## [Unreleased]` into `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD` in `CHANGELOG.md` and set `VERSION`. While 0.x: minor for features or breaking changes, patch for fixes, chores and docs.
3. Commit, push, `gh pr create --base main` with `Closes #<issue>`.
4. `gh pr checks <pr> --watch` until green. Never merge red.
5. `gh pr merge <pr> --squash --delete-branch`, then `git checkout main; git pull --ff-only`.
6. Release the merge commit:

   ```powershell
   git tag -a vX.Y.Z -m "vX.Y.Z" <merge-sha>; git push origin vX.Y.Z
   gh release create vX.Y.Z --title "vX.Y.Z" --notes "<CHANGELOG section>"
   ```

7. Deploy to production (`npo-workdash.apes.org.uk`, app `b253bb6f-f66a-49cc-aa7f-79464eebdc91`):

   ```powershell
   & "C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe" deploy/cloudron/cloudron-deploy.sh vX.Y.Z
   ```

   It must end with `/up` returning 200 and the live `REVISION` matching. If it fails, read the output, fix or roll back (`docs/deploy/cloudron.md`), and report it.
8. Report: PR link, short merge SHA, release link, deploy evidence, issues closed.

Do not claim a step happened without its command output.
